    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0627" n="509" xml:id="pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/855</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d495-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg leave, adverting to your despatch No.
                    5550, of July 10, 1928, and your radio message No. 251, of August 2, 1
                        p.m.,<anchor n="61" xml:id="d495-f2"/> both concerning the surtax on
                    imported coal imposed at Shanghai, to inform you that although this tax is
                    nominally a consumption tax, from the fact, as stated in your despatch, that it
                    is imposed on coal imported by an American firm, it appears to the Legation that
                    it partakes of the nature of a surtax on imports. For this reason you are
                    authorized, should such a course now appear to you advisable, to enter a protest
                    against its imposition.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. V. A.
                    MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d495-f1" n="60" type="source" xml:id="d495-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Chargé in China in his despatch No.
                    1608, August 13; received September 15.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d495-f2" n="61" xml:id="d495-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
